{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.qbeta_channel_split","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.qbeta_channel_split","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaChannelSplit.barEven_remainder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaChannelSplit.barEven_remainder","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_channel_split.lean#L49-L55","doc":"The bar-even remainder: `ε(Δ) − barOdd = barEven`. This is the internal\n`h²/2` term; it is part of the counit `Q_β`, **not** a separate binding\ncontribution (the earlier \"double-count\" reading is refuted by the #2346\n`Im 𝔙 = ` full-counit witness — see file header). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaChannelSplit.barOdd_anti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaChannelSplit.barOdd_anti","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_channel_split.lean#L45-L47","doc":"`barOdd` is negated under the bar-involution `h ↦ −h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaChannelSplit.barEven_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaChannelSplit.barEven_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_channel_split.lean#L41-L43","doc":"`barEven` is invariant under the bar-involution `h ↦ −h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaChannelSplit.counit_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaChannelSplit.counit_split","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_channel_split.lean#L35-L39","doc":"The counit `ε(Δ) = h²/2 − h` is the sum of its bar-even and bar-odd\nparts. (Internal decomposition; both parts belong to the counit / `Q_β`,\nper the branch-A resolution — see file header.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaChannelSplit.barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaChannelSplit.barOdd","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_channel_split.lean#L32-L33","doc":"Bar-odd part of the counit on the nucleon difference, `−h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaChannelSplit.barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaChannelSplit.barEven","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_channel_split.lean#L29-L30","doc":"Bar-even part of the counit on the nucleon difference, `h²/2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}